        "note_request_suggestions": [
          {
            "source_link": "https://x.com/R2Cdev_/status/2089623261843730573",
            "suggestion": "This comparison is misleading because the two displayed prices do not represent the same thing.\n\no1-pro was a separately priced model: its $150/M input and $600/M output rates directly reflected the premium Pro model.\n\nSince GPT-5.6, “Pro” is instead a reasoning mode applied to the regular GPT-5.6 model. GPT-5.6 Sol Pro therefore uses Sol’s normal token rates ($5/M input, $30/M output), but Pro mode performs and bills substantially more internal model work to produce an answer. OpenRouter’s current 50% promotion simply reduces those base rates to $2.50/$15.\n\nSo comparing o1-pro’s $150/$600 directly with GPT-5.6 Sol Pro’s $2.50/$15 gives a misleading impression of the reduction in the actual cost of a Pro response.\n\nOpenAI explains the new Pro-mode billing here:\nhttps://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning#reasoning-mode",
            "suggestion_id": "2089702294619033949"
          }
        ],
